 18 June 2015 APPENDIX 1 SELECTION OF BILLS COMMITTEE Proposal to refer a bill to a committee: Name of bill: Australian Small Business and Family Enterprise Ombudsman Bill 2015 Reasons for referral/principal issues for consideration: The role and operation of the small business Ombudsman seem inconsistent with the operation of similar Ombudsman positions. Possible submissions or evidence from: Relevant small business stakeholders Committee to which bill is to be referred: Legal and Constitutional Affairs Possible hearing date(s): To be determined by the committee Possible reporting date: 11 August 2015 (signed) Senator Anne McEwen I move: That the report be adopted. Gavin Marshall The question is that that motion be agreed to. Claire Moore Mr Deputy President, we have an amendment to the Selection of Bills Committee report. I move the amendment which has been circulated in the chamber: At the end of the motion, add, \"but, in respect of the Australian Small Business and Family Enterprise ","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3815","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-06-18/1"}
